    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0667" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/192: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece (MacVeagh) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-11-01T15:00:00+02:00">November 1, 1933—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 1—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. Grounds of refusal cannot be definitely stated till we have had a chance to
                    study documents. Decision apparently admits acts committed were violations of
                    the law in both countries but contends that the proof of criminal intent so far
                    submitted is insufficient. The prosecutor told Harness this morning that he
                    believes the way is thus left open for introduction of new evidence and
                    reopening the case and he is now preparing memorandum on this subject after
                    conference with Solicitor General. Will advise further very shortly. I am seeing
                    Foreign Minister this afternoon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
